  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PreCare 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "A research team is choosing which treatment options to test next. Through
    surveys and advisory groups, you and other caregivers share that long-lasting
    fatigue and \u201Cbrain fog\u201D make it hard for patients to keep up with daily
    life and stay independent.\n\n<b>Preclinical studies focus on how well a treatment
    works\u2014researchers don\u2019t watch for side effects until clinical trials
    begin.</b>\n\nIs this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?"
  explanation: "Even in preclinical research, scientists look for possible side effects
    while testing new treatments. Caregiver feedback about issues like fatigue or
    \u201Cbrain fog\u201D helps researchers know what to monitor from the start.
    This early attention can prevent treatments with serious quality-of-life concerns
    from moving forward unnecessarily."
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: PreClinical
